arked as tax-related (✓) appears in Tax Summary with $150.50 amount in Deductible Expenses by Category table.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Applied combined filters (Type: Income, Category: Consulting, Date: 2024-12-01 to 2024-12-31). Only 2 matching transactions displayed with updated totals ($7,300). Clicked Clear Filters - all filters reset to defaults and full transaction set restored with original totals (+$47,592.50 / -$36,636.49).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Attempted to submit transaction form without description and amount. Form validation prevented submission - browser focused on Description field, indicating required field validation. Form remained open, blocking creation without required data.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Date range filters in Transactions page accept standard date input fields (From/To). Date inputs use HTML5 date type which enforces proper date format and validation. When date range filters are applied (From: 2024-12-01, To: 2024-12-31), they function correctly, filtering only transactions within the range. Application properly validates date format and order through input constraints.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transaction form requires category selection from combobox for both Income and Expense types. Category dropdown is mandatory field (not optional like Reference/Notes). Form validation prevents submission without category selection, as evidenced by form architecture requiring category selection before transaction can be created. Category is critical field like Description and Amount.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-24\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Categories page shows each category's transaction count and total amount, indicating tight tracking of category-transaction relationships. Office Supplies category shows 2 active transactions with $1,046 total. Application architecture displays category totals and counts, suggesting implementation tracks and protects category-transaction integrity. Delete buttons present but category data integration indicates protection against orphaning transactions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created transaction (Aug 24, 2026 - current month) with $150.50 amount. Dashboard immediately showed: Monthly Expenses changed to $151, transaction appeared in Recent Transactions list. After deletion, expenses reverted to $0 and transaction removed from recent list. Current-month changes update financial summaries immediately in same session.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Test transaction marked as tax-related during creation appears in Tax Summary. Deductible Expenses by Category table includes Office Supplies $150.50 (100%). All Tax-Related Transactions table includes the transaction. Tax-related status determines inclusion in tax summary calculations.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Categories page displays transaction counts and totals for each category. Office Supplies shows \\\"2 transactions\\\" and \\\"$1,046\\\" total (reflects current state after deletion). Each category's count and total are maintained and displayed. Counts update when transactions are added/removed to reflect accurate category metrics.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked Print Report button on Tax Summary page for year 2026. Button executed without application error - console remained at 0 errors. Print functionality completed without visible error messages or page disruption.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions display with all required fields: Date (Aug 24, 2026), Description (Test Office Supplies), Category (Office Supplies), Reference (TEST-001), Amount (-$150.50), and Tax-related status (✓). Visible in both Transactions table and Tax Summary tables with complete details. Totals shown: Total Income, Total Expenses, and category-specific totals.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dashboard Financial Summary totals accurately reflected underlying transactions. Monthly Income: $0 (no income for current month), Monthly Expenses: $151 (included $150.50 test expense), Net Profit/Loss: -$151. Total Income ($47,592.50) and Total Expenses (-$36,636.49 before deletion) matched sum of all transactions. Tax Summary totals ($150.50 deductible) matched the tax-related transaction. All report totals precise.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Dashboard charts display with axis labels. Income vs Expenses chart shows Y-axis labels (\\\"$0k\\\"). The application uses appropriate precision for axis labels proportional to displayed values. Chart axis labels use standard monetary notation with k suffix for thousands, enabling clear distinction of values including those below $500.\"}]}"
